    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date behavior for `POST /api/owners`: when no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and the field is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this generates the field on both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) as `java.time.LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` entity** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `Pet.birthDate` pattern.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after mapping the request, defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the client didn't supply one. A supplied date passes through unchanged (verified by the `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` test).\n\n4. **Schema DDL** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **Seed data** (`hsqldb`, `mysql` `data.sql`) \u2014 the positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` statements needed a trailing `NULL` for the new column; the h2/postgres inserts already use explicit column lists so they were unaffected.\n\nMapStruct maps the field by name automatically, so `OwnerMapper` needed no change, and the PUT path's `ApplyOwner` mutates in place without touching `registrationDate`, so existing values are preserved on update.",
